## The robot

I used `carter_v1` from the NVIDIA asset library and referenced it into the
scene. It already ships with a 32-beam LiDAR (`XT_32_10Hz`) and four cameras, so
I didn't need to bolt sensors on manually. I spawned it at the start of the
centre lane and set its Z to about 0.3 m so it sits on the ground instead of
clipping into it.

For driving, I built this in the Action Graph:

```
On Playback Tick → Differential Controller → Articulation Controller → wheels
```

- Differential Controller: wheel radius 0.24, wheel distance 0.54, forward speed
  set through desiredLinearVelocity.
- Articulation Controller: pointed at `/World/carter_v1`, driving the
  `left_wheel` and `right_wheel` joints.

Forward and reverse both work (reverse is just a negative speed — the wheels are
oriented so negative actually drives it up the lane into the field).

