## Sensors / ROS 2

Everything publishes through one Action Graph that shares a single tick and one
ROS 2 context.

**`/clock`** was the first thing I got working — once that showed up in
`ros2 topic list`, I knew the ROS 2 bridge was actually connected end to end.

**`/scan`** (the LiDAR) took a bit more. In 6.0.1 you can't just point the LiDAR
helper at the sensor prim — it errors with "unknown render product." The fix was
to add an **Isaac Create Render Product** node, set its cameraPrim to the LiDAR
(`/World/carter_v1/chassis_link/XT_32_10Hz`), and feed its render-product output
into the helper. After that `/scan` publishes fine while the sim is playing.

Graph shape:

```
On Playback Tick ─┬─ ROS2 Publish Clock          (← ROS2 Context)
                  ├─ Render Product → RTX Lidar Helper   (← ROS2 Context)
                  ├─ Differential Controller → Articulation Controller
                  └─ camera render product + camera helper  (partial)
```

