## Physics stuff I had to fix

- **Robot kept falling through the floor.** The first ground was just a flat
  mesh with no collision. Giving it a convex-hull collider made a bad thin
  collision shape, and the rigid-body preset made the ground itself fall (robot
  and ground dropped together, which was funny but not useful). What actually
  worked was deleting it and using a proper physics ground plane
  (`Create > Physics > Ground Plane`) — that's a static floor by default.
- Keep the robot's spawn Z a bit above 0 so it doesn't start inside the ground.

