## Known issues

- **Camera ROS 2 publishing isn't finished.** I added the camera helper and its
  render product but didn't fully wire/test it, and a half-connected render
  product throws a "render product not valid" warning that can stall the graph.
  If you just want to see what the camera sees, open a second viewport and set
  its camera to `carter_camera_first_person` — no ROS 2 needed.
- The `fullScan is deprecated` warning is harmless (the setting is ignored). Can
  be turned off by unchecking Publish Full Scan.
- The plants have no collision, so the robot won't physically bump into them —
  fine for a driving demo, would need colliders for real crop interaction.
- The crops are stylised, not photoreal.
- The ground is currently plain/untextured — cosmetic, easy to fix later.

