## Why the crops are hand-built (the asset search)

Keeping this here so nobody repeats the hunt:

- Sketchfab "cotton" is mostly home-decor (cotton stems in vases), broken
  photogrammetry scans, or paid Store assets. The free ones I checked were
  either fused multi-object scenes, decorative rather than agricultural, or
  huge (one single plant was ~880k triangles).
- Poly Haven has no crop plant.
- CropCraft (Romea, Apache-2.0) is a solid procedural field generator and I got
  it installed and running, but it doesn't ship plant models and its labels are
  crop/weed, not healthy/dead — so not the fastest route here.
- The academic cotton repos I found either ship only textures (no mesh) or have
  no licence at all.

So I built the plants and field as USD directly. No licence risk, low poly,
exact spacing, and easy per-plant healthy/dead control. The trade-off is the
plants are simple/stylised rather than realistic.

